bmake prints the location of a diagnostic as `<file>:<line>:` since
bmake-20260824; it used to print `"<file>" line <n>:`.

tests/reqd, reqd2, reqd3 and reqd4 strip that location off the nested
make's error line before diffing it against expect.out, and
examples/helpers/mkc_test_helper strips it off every test's output (the
test_subprj_dash, reqd_clean_cache and reqd_clean_cache2 recipes, and
every example, pipe through it).  Both know only the old spelling, so
with the new one the location survived and the message was then cut off
by the trailing `s/".*//`, or was compared away from its expected bare
form; %check failed on every arch.

Strip up to the last `: "` instead, which matches both spellings.  The
old expression is kept so the helper still copes with older bmake.

--- a/examples/helpers/mkc_test_helper	2026-10-14 22:42:43.000000000 +0200
+++ b/examples/helpers/mkc_test_helper	2026-10-16 19:06:41.314760620 +0200
@@ -46,5 +46,6 @@
     -e 's,lua/[0-9]*[.][0-9]*,lua/X.Y,' \
     -e 's,//,/,g' \
     -e 's,^bmake:.*line [0-9][0-9]*: "\(.*\)".*$,\1,g' \
+    -e 's,^bmake:[^"]*:[0-9][0-9]*: "\(.*\)".*$,\1,g' \
     -e 's/[.]sl/.so/' -e /so_locations/d |
 $SORT_CMD
--- a/tests/reqd/test.mk	2026-10-14 22:42:43.000000000 +0200
+++ b/tests/reqd/test.mk	2026-10-16 18:57:17.823552977 +0200
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 	rm -f $$tmp_out; \
 	${MAKE} all MKC_REQD=999.0.0 2>&1 | head -1 | \
 	sed -e 's/ [0-9][0-9]*[.][0-9][0-9]*[.][0-9][0-9]*/ N.N.N/' \
-		-e 's/^.* line[^"]*"//' -e 's/".*//' > $$tmp_out; \
+		-e 's/^.*: "//' -e 's/".*//' > $$tmp_out; \
 	diff ${.CURDIR}/expect.out $$tmp_out && \
 	echo '      succeeded' 1>&2 || \
 	{ echo '      FAILED' 1>&2; false; }
